//! Turn structure: `end_player_turn`, `_run_enemy_phase`, `monster_act`, and
//! `begin_player_turn`.
//!
//! `end_player_turn` (frozen Python, deleted #2827) is one action from the caller's point of view
//! but four Python phases: the auto-post phase marker, the turn-end-in-hand /
//! Ethereal wrappers and the hand flush, the side switch and enemy phase, and
//! the next turn's start. They are kept as four functions here for the same
//! reason Python keeps them: the enemy phase is separately resumable
//! (`_run_enemy_phase(stage, remaining_uids)`), and the resume path lands
//! exactly where the stages meet.
//!
//! Almost all of the ~400 lines of Python side-end bookkeeping is listener
//! dispatch over powers and relics the admission gate refuses. What survives
//! is named below at the point it runs, so a later slice adds a call rather
//! than discovering that a step was silently missing.

